1. OWNERSHIP AND INTELLECTUAL PROPERTY RIGHTS (GERMAN & EU LAW)
================================================================================
This website, software portfolio, and all associated projects — including all
source code, algorithms, system architectures, database schemas, user interface
designs, CSS design systems, 3D/interactive simulations, telemetry pipelines,
graphics, texts, and bilingual CV documents comprising the "Ali Sibai
Engineering Portfolio", "SpaceLumin / Lumin Flow: Utopia Run", and "SmartPark
Guardian AI / Smart Parking Management System (PMS)" (collectively, the
"Protected Works") — are the original creation and exclusive intellectual
property of Ali Sibai.

The Protected Works are legally protected under:
- The German Copyright Act (Gesetz über Urheberrecht und verwandte Schutzrechte —
  Urheberrechtsgesetz, UrhG), in particular:
  * §§ 2 Abs. 1 Nr. 1, 4, 7 & 69a UrhG (Protection of computer programs,
    literary/technical works, and web design architecture);
  * §§ 12–14 & 29 UrhG (Urheberpersönlichkeitsrecht / Inalienable moral rights
    of authorship);
  * §§ 15–23, 19a & 69c UrhG (Exclusive rights of reproduction, adaptation,
    distribution, and making available to the public);
  * §§ 87a–87e UrhG (Protection of databases and structured data);
  * §§ 95a & 95c UrhG (Protection of technological measures and copyright
    management information);
  * §§ 97, 97a, 106 & 108a UrhG (Civil injunctive relief, damages, and criminal
    penalties for unauthorized reproduction or commercial exploitation);
- The German Act Against Unfair Competition (Gesetz gegen den unlauteren
  Wettbewerb — UWG), in particular § 4 Nr. 3 UWG (Prohibition of commercial
  imitation, cloning, and misappropriation of reputation / Nachahmungsschutz);
- European Union Copyright Directives:
  * Directive 2009/24/EC on the legal protection of computer programs;
  * Directive 2001/29/EC (InfoSoc Directive);
  * Directive (EU) 2019/790 (DSM Directive), including explicit reservation of
    rights pursuant to Article 4(3) and § 44b Abs. 3 UrhG; and
- The Berne Convention for the Protection of Literary and Artistic Works (Art.
  6bis) and the WIPO Copyright Treaty (WCT).

Under §§ 12–14 and § 29 UrhG, the authorship (Urheberschaft) of Ali Sibai is
legally inalienable and cannot be transferred, waived, or appropriated by any
third party.

